.TH TRAVERSE 1 "January 30, 2026"
.SH NAME
traverse \- print indented list of files in a specified directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
traverse a directory and show the files that \fIshar\fP(1) would process.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I traverse
is a simple program
using the traverse() function from the \fIshar\fP sources to print the 
tab indented list of files that \fIshar\fP(1) would process.
.sp
If the argument is a directory,
then traverse applies func to all its entries.
This traversal is in depth first order
so that files are processed in the order
that they are stored in the directory.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
traverse /var
/var/
	db/
		find.codes
	run/
		dev.dir
		syslog.pid
		dev.pag
		psdatabase
		utmp
		cron.pid
		acctd.pid
	log/
		learn/
			C
			editor
			eqn
			files
			macros
			morefiles
			vi
		sendmail.st
	cron/
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Gary Perlman
.SH BUGS
There are no diagnostics when directories cannot be searched.
